{
  "title": "Enrich endpoint swallows all errors (including DB failures) into \
'return original tags'",
  "description": "server/src/api/enrich.rs:88 try_enrich_tags is documented \
'Returns the original tags on any failure', and enrich_recipe \
(enrich.rs:62-68) collapses every error — DB connection failure, AI outage, \
tag-fetch failure — into a warn! and returns unmodified tags. A DB error is \
indistinguishable from 'AI unavailable', violating the repo's fail-fast \
policy. build_registry similarly falls back via \
fetch_user_tags(...).unwrap_or_else(...) at server/src/scraping/mod.rs:211.\n\
\n\
Fix: surface DB/internal errors as 500s; only degrade (explicitly) for genuine \
AI-unavailability, and make that case distinguishable in the response or logs. \
Partly a policy call on which failures may degrade — decide per case, but \
silent blanket fallback should go.\n\
\n\
Both clients call enrich; neither needs UI changes beyond whatever error they \
already render for 5xx. No pipeline data/ diffs expected.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "api",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-02T05:30:02-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-07-02T05:30:02-07:00",
}
